# Netlify headers - caches everything under / for 1 year
# NOTE: This sets Cache-Control for all paths under / to 1 year. Make sure you use
# cache-busting (e.g. file fingerprinting or query string versioning) for assets
# that change, or users may keep stale copies for up to 1 year.
/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Safer alternative (commented out):
# - Set long caching for static assets (images, css, js), and short/no cache for HTML
# Uncomment and use instead of the rule above if you don't fingerprint files.
